{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-23T17:18:12.801Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"68fbab5beab3a8962120e4ae","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/5","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-23T17:18:12.801Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Blocking review follow-up: JSON serialization drops undefined values from session patches, hiding field removals in saved watcher proposals. Encode removals explicitly at the watcher persistence boundary, document the representation, and add a real no-git tracker regression removing a due token. Prove the regression fails with only that encoding fix reverted, restore it, run targeted tests, typecheck and configured lint, and wait for fresh npm/Bun CI release gates. Remote feature head is unchanged and main has not advanced."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-23T17:18:12.801Z"}],"before_hash":"be204f33c1c474b52a9d4671791aeaddfd605d285e7c56390bb3c25890fe9644","after_hash":"ed5a93abb51c296a11de408a0b7672350b1a27b2d418c0e689297fc71802ed81","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"1c8e5e74a086c510e98bbcfda1e1423e78e53a55e13ed993199b198046acef31"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-23T17:21:38.662Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"68fbab5beab3a8962120e4ae","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/6","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-23T17:21:38.662Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Blocking PR 144 finding fixed: persisted TodoProposalPatch now separates defined set values from an explicit removedFields list, so deleting due:2026-12-01 records deadline removal in proposals.json. Queue/proposal schema 2 and versioned proposal ids prevent pre-fix version 1 evidence being silently reused; legacy queues return spool_mismatch and are preserved for archival. README and SDK example document set/remove semantics and migration. Regression: watcher persists due-token removal as an explicit deadline field removal, using a real non-git SDK tracker with git absent from PATH. Isolated test passed; reverting only persistablePatches to retain undefined values and an empty removal list failed the saved deadline-removal assertion (1 failure), then the encoder was restored. Final pm test --run --progress passed both linked commands: 19 watcher tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations; npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run docstring and git diff --check passed. Fresh exact-head npm/Bun release gates will be linked with counts in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/pull/144."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-23T17:21:38.662Z"}],"before_hash":"ed5a93abb51c296a11de408a0b7672350b1a27b2d418c0e689297fc71802ed81","after_hash":"6da880e5c687e90f9b84375ac86048f0540dab53ff4b1cddf5aa345810ee60d2","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule